24
00:01:24,660 --> 00:01:27,220
Before anything else, I
would like to highlight the

25
00:01:27,220 --> 00:01:30,580
most important features of
valvular disease in general.

26
00:01:30,760 --> 00:01:34,680
Valvular disease might present
as valvular stenosis or

27
00:01:34,680 --> 00:01:38,500
insufficiency. Some patients
might present with both

28
00:01:38,500 --> 00:01:42,620
vulvular stenosis or
insufficiency in the same valve.

29
00:01:43,480 --> 00:01:47,400
Vulvular stenosis it
represents failure of a valve

30
00:01:47,400 --> 00:01:51,480
to open completely obstructing
forward blood flow.

31
00:01:52,200 --> 00:01:55,600
It is determined by a
primary cuspal pathological

32
00:01:55,600 --> 00:02:00,220
process such as calcification
or valve scaring.

33
00:02:00,900 --> 00:02:03,020
Valvular insufficiency

34
00:02:04,180 --> 00:02:07,100
Valvular insufficiency
represents failure

35
00:02:07,100 --> 00:02:11,340
of a valve to close
completely As a result,

36
00:02:11,440 --> 00:02:15,620
there is regurgitation
or backflow of blood

37
00:02:16,560 --> 00:02:20,280
This is determined by
a disease of the valve

38
00:02:20,280 --> 00:02:24,280
cusps such as endocarditis
or a destruction

39
00:02:24,280 --> 00:02:27,600
of the valvular
supporting apparatus the

40
00:02:27,600 --> 00:02:30,220
tendinous cords and
the papillary muscle.

41
00:02:33,420 --> 00:02:36,320
Some patients might
present with valvular

42
00:02:36,320 --> 00:02:39,840
pathology in one valve
or in several valves.

43
00:02:40,100 --> 00:02:42,380
Anyway, the most
commonly affected

44
00:02:42,380 --> 00:02:44,520
valve is the mitral valve.

45
00:02:45,620 --> 00:02:48,700
Usually, these patients
will present with a

46
00:02:48,700 --> 00:02:52,060
murmur, which is determined
by a turbulent flow

47
00:02:52,060 --> 00:02:56,100
through the diseased
valve. However, if the

48
00:02:56,100 --> 00:02:59,940
stenosis is severe,
thrills might be palpated.

49
00:03:01,200 --> 00:03:04,340
The outcome. The outcome
in these patients

50
00:03:04,340 --> 00:03:07,240
depends on the valve
or the valves affected,

51
00:03:07,380 --> 00:03:10,280
the degree of impairment and

52
00:03:10,280 --> 00:03:12,040
the tempo of its development.

53
00:03:12,760 --> 00:03:17,260
In addition, the
outcome is determined by

54
00:03:17,260 --> 00:03:21,900
compensatory mechanisms.
For example, cardiac

55
00:03:21,900 --> 00:03:23,940
failure might
develop after a rapid

56
00:03:23,940 --> 00:03:26,740
destruction of aortic
valve by an infection.

57
00:03:27,060 --> 00:03:28,540
By contrast,

58
00:03:28,880 --> 00:03:32,580
rheumatic mitral stenosis
develops very slowly.

59
00:03:32,680 --> 00:03:36,480
In these cases, clinical
effects are well tolerated

60
00:03:36,480 --> 00:03:39,460
until late in the
evolution of the disease.

61
00:03:40,930 --> 00:03:44,140
Now let's summarize the
most important aspects

62
00:03:44,140 --> 00:03:47,100
related to the etiology
of cardiac valvulopathies.

63
00:03:47,580 --> 00:03:50,380
There are two types
of valvulopathies,

64
00:03:50,380 --> 00:03:52,380
congenital and acquired.

65
00:03:52,920 --> 00:03:56,360
The most common
congenital valvulopathy is

66
00:03:56,360 --> 00:04:00,500
the bicuspid aortic
valve stenosis and the

67
00:04:00,500 --> 00:04:03,480
most common acquired
valvulopathies are

68
00:04:03,480 --> 00:04:06,920
represented by aortic
and mitral stenosis.

69
00:04:08,500 --> 00:04:11,520
These pathological
conditions represent

70
00:04:11,520 --> 00:04:13,900
two-thirds of all
valvulopathies.

71
00:04:17,090 --> 00:04:21,600
As mentioned in the right
-side table, the most

72
00:04:21,600 --> 00:04:25,280
important cause of both
mitral and aortic stenosis

73
00:04:25,280 --> 00:04:29,180
is represented by
rheumatic heart disease.

74
00:04:29,840 --> 00:04:34,220
At this stage, we will
not cover the less common

75
00:04:34,220 --> 00:04:38,220
conditions related to mitral
and aortic regurgitation

76
00:04:38,220 --> 00:04:41,940
except mitral valve
prolapse and mitral annular

77
00:04:41,940 --> 00:04:45,240
calcification or
calcification of mitral ring.

78
00:04:45,920 --> 00:04:47,120
However,

79
00:04:47,780 --> 00:04:51,180
all these entities are
enumerated in this table.

80
00:04:56,310 --> 00:04:57,770
Calcific aortic stenosis

81
00:04:58,530 --> 00:05:01,170
Calcific aortic
stenosis is the most

82
00:05:01,170 --> 00:05:03,410
common cause of
aortic stenosis.

83
00:05:03,710 --> 00:05:06,250
It may be asymptomatic
and is seen

84
00:05:06,250 --> 00:05:09,590
incidentally during
routine chest X-ray.

85
00:05:09,870 --> 00:05:13,490
However, some patients
present with severe

86
00:05:13,490 --> 00:05:16,650
symptomatology and
require surgical therapy.

87
00:05:17,350 --> 00:05:20,530
In subjects with normal
valves, it manifests

88
00:05:20,530 --> 00:05:23,610
around 78 years of
age, while in those

89
00:05:23,610 --> 00:05:26,390
with congenital
bicuspid valves is

90
00:05:26,390 --> 00:05:30,110
diagnosed earlier, around
40-50 years of age.

91
00:05:31,370 --> 00:05:32,710
Pathogenesis.

92
00:05:33,270 --> 00:05:36,930
Although simple
progressive age-associated

93
00:05:36,930 --> 00:05:40,230
wear and tear
mechanism is usually

94
00:05:40,230 --> 00:05:42,530
the explanation
for this condition,

95
00:05:43,150 --> 00:05:46,390
cuspal fibrosis and
calcification, which are observed

96
00:05:46,390 --> 00:05:50,190
in aortic stenosis,
could be regarded as the

97
00:05:50,190 --> 00:05:53,570
valvular equivalent of age
-related atherosclerosis.

98
00:05:55,250 --> 00:05:58,610
Therefore atherosclerosis
risk factors

99
00:05:58,610 --> 00:06:01,990
such as hyperlipidemia,
hypertension

100
00:06:02,620 --> 00:06:05,770
and chronic inflammation
are also regarded

101
00:06:05,770 --> 00:06:09,070
as risk factors for
calcific aortic stenosis.

102
00:06:11,760 --> 00:06:15,450
On the right upper side
of this slide we have

103
00:06:15,450 --> 00:06:18,430
several examples of
calcific aortic stenosis.

104
00:06:18,830 --> 00:06:20,790
In image A,

105
00:06:20,970 --> 00:06:23,870
we have a case of
calcific aortic

106
00:06:23,870 --> 00:06:27,110
stenosis in a
previously normal valve.

107
00:06:27,230 --> 00:06:30,850
In this setting, there are
numerous nodular masses

108
00:06:30,850 --> 00:06:34,670
