136
00:08:31,830 --> 00:08:35,890
Calcific aortic stenosis
histology On this

137
00:08:35,890 --> 00:08:39,270
slide, we have an image
showing a standard

138
00:08:39,270 --> 00:08:43,330
hematoxilineosin state
section, which was performed

139
00:08:43,330 --> 00:08:46,070
through a heavily
calcified aortic valve.

140
00:08:46,390 --> 00:08:50,150
You can see the calcium
deposits appearing as empty

141
00:08:50,150 --> 00:08:54,750
spaces as calcium was removed
during tissue processing.

142
00:08:55,210 --> 00:08:58,070
Anyway, it is believed
that calcification

143
00:08:58,070 --> 00:09:00,530
begins at the base
of the aortic valve.

144
00:09:01,010 --> 00:09:04,710
Eventually, this abnormal
process will lead to

145
00:09:04,710 --> 00:09:07,410
a reduction in the actual
valve functional area.

146
00:09:09,230 --> 00:09:13,550
This reduction is
associated with an outflow

147
00:09:13,550 --> 00:09:17,210
obstruction and pressure
overload as the heart will

148
00:09:17,210 --> 00:09:20,010
have to push blood against
an increased pressure.

149
00:09:22,650 --> 00:09:25,350
Aortic stenosis
physiopathology.

150
00:09:25,510 --> 00:09:28,810
As mentioned before,
calcific aortic stenosis

151
00:09:28,810 --> 00:09:32,610
may be age-related or
senile, or it may develop

152
00:09:32,610 --> 00:09:36,130
on a bicuspid valve.
This calcified valve will

153
00:09:36,130 --> 00:09:38,890
determine obstruction and
narrowing of the aorta.

154
00:09:39,440 --> 00:09:41,970
This will lead to an
increased pressure

155
00:09:41,970 --> 00:09:45,430
gradient, which in
turn will be associated

156
00:09:45,430 --> 00:09:47,910
with an increased left
ventricular pressure.

157
00:09:48,370 --> 00:09:49,830
In time,

158
00:09:50,050 --> 00:09:51,950
these patients will
develop cardiac

159
00:09:51,950 --> 00:09:54,170
hypertrophy and
cardiac failure.

160
00:09:54,990 --> 00:09:57,570
Patients with
cardiac hypertrophy

161
00:09:57,950 --> 00:10:00,210
will subsequently present with

162
00:10:00,210 --> 00:10:03,870
events such as
angina and syncope.

163
00:10:04,690 --> 00:10:09,690
All of these features
indicate cardiac ischemia and

164
00:10:09,690 --> 00:10:13,690
a severe decreased
compensatory cardiac function.

165
00:10:15,760 --> 00:10:18,850
Prolapse In this
setting, one or both

166
00:10:18,850 --> 00:10:21,130
mitral leaflets are
floppy and prolapse

167
00:10:21,130 --> 00:10:23,090
back into the atrium
during systole.

168
00:10:23,570 --> 00:10:25,870
Mitral valve prolapse
is associated with

169
00:10:25,870 --> 00:10:27,990
conditions characterized
by connective

170
00:10:27,990 --> 00:10:31,430
tissue pathology, such
as Marfan syndrome,

171
00:10:31,730 --> 00:10:34,890
Ehlers-Danlos syndrome,
as well as polycystic

172
00:10:34,890 --> 00:10:37,370
kidney disease and
fragile X syndrome.

173
00:10:38,230 --> 00:10:39,150
Ethiology.

174
00:10:40,150 --> 00:10:42,550
Mitral valve prolapse
is determined

175
00:10:42,550 --> 00:10:44,130
by myxomatous degeneration,

176
00:10:44,410 --> 00:10:46,750
which represents
the deposition of

177
00:10:46,750 --> 00:10:48,650
abnormal material
in the valves.

178
00:10:48,960 --> 00:10:52,730
This can be spontaneous
or primary or secondary to

179
00:10:52,730 --> 00:10:57,010
a connective tissue
disorder. It is also seen in

180
00:10:57,010 --> 00:11:00,250
rheumatic fever and after
myocardial infarction.

181
00:11:01,610 --> 00:11:02,890
Pathogenesis.

182
00:11:03,530 --> 00:11:06,810
In myxomatoid degeneration
of mitral valve,

183
00:11:06,810 --> 00:11:09,630
the leaflets show an
excessive degradation of

184
00:11:09,630 --> 00:11:13,050
collagen and elastin
by proteolytic enzymes.

185
00:11:13,450 --> 00:11:15,230
There is also a significant

186
00:11:15,230 --> 00:11:18,170
accumulation of
abnormal proteoglycans.

187
00:11:20,010 --> 00:11:23,490
As a result of all
these, the corded

188
00:11:23,490 --> 00:11:24,850
tendinale will have an abnormal

189
00:11:24,850 --> 00:11:29,310
plasticity, they become
weak and elongated

190
00:11:29,830 --> 00:11:34,270
In addition, there is
also annular dilatation

191
00:11:34,270 --> 00:11:37,790
of the mitral valve
On the other hand,

192
00:11:38,050 --> 00:11:40,170
in connective tissue disorders,

193
00:11:40,410 --> 00:11:44,230
there is deficiency
of normal collagen as

194
00:11:44,230 --> 00:11:47,890
well as a low level
of velocity And the

195
00:11:47,890 --> 00:11:51,010
leaflets are becoming
thin and translucent

196
00:11:53,630 --> 00:11:57,250
Let's describe the
morphological changes associated

197
00:11:57,250 --> 00:12:01,190
with mitral valve
prolapse As you can see

198
00:12:01,190 --> 00:12:05,450
in this macroscopic
image on the left side of

199
00:12:05,450 --> 00:12:08,810
this slide The mitral
valve will prolapse back

200
00:12:08,810 --> 00:12:11,330
into the left atrium
during cardiac contraction

201
00:12:12,150 --> 00:12:14,930
In some cases, the patient

202
00:12:14,930 --> 00:12:18,470
might develop
atrial dilatation.

203
00:12:18,610 --> 00:12:21,510
This is determined by
valvular insufficiency,

204
00:12:21,510 --> 00:12:24,330
which develops late in
the course of the disease.

205
00:12:24,750 --> 00:12:29,010
The right side image
represents two histological

206
00:12:29,010 --> 00:12:31,810
images, a normal
cardiac valve and a

207
00:12:31,810 --> 00:12:34,670
section taken from a
myxomatous mitral valve.

208
00:12:35,220 --> 00:12:38,710
In the diseased structure,
you can see that its

209
00:12:38,710 --> 00:12:42,630
architecture is severely
disorganized with loosely disposed

210
00:12:42,630 --> 00:12:46,960
collagen in the fibrosa
layer There is also abnormal

211
00:12:46,960 --> 00:12:50,450
proteoglycan in spongiosa
layer of the mitral valve

212
00:12:54,330 --> 00:12:58,590
I would also like to discuss
very briefly the mitral

213
00:12:58,590 --> 00:13:01,110
annular classification,
a condition seen in

214
00:13:01,110 --> 00:13:03,730
patients with myxomatous
degeneration of the mitral

215
00:13:03,730 --> 00:13:07,210
valve but most of the time
an incidental finding.

216
00:13:07,730 --> 00:13:11,790
Usually these patients are
women over 60 years of age

217
00:13:11,790 --> 00:13:16,070
with mitral var prolapse or
any other cardiac pathology

218
00:13:16,070 --> 00:13:19,430
associated with increased
left ventricular pressure.

219
00:13:20,970 --> 00:13:22,170
Pathogenesis.

220
00:13:22,680 --> 00:13:26,230
As you may see in this
image, this condition is

221
00:13:26,230 --> 00:13:29,570
characterized by numerous
irregular hard nodules

222
00:13:29,570 --> 00:13:34,270
representing degenerative
calcific deposits at the base

223
00:13:34,270 --> 00:13:38,930
of the leaflets sometimes
this might be ulcerated

224
00:13:39,890 --> 00:13:42,770
mitral annular
calcification most of

225
00:13:42,770 --> 00:13:45,250
the time requires
no specific therapy

226
00:13:45,590 --> 00:13:47,910
however the
associated conditions

227
00:13:47,910 --> 00:13:50,070
such as mitral valve prolapse

228
00:13:50,190 --> 00:13:54,230
stenosis and or
regurgitation as well as the

229
00:13:54,230 --> 00:13:56,270
conditions which lead
to increased left

230
00:13:56,270 --> 00:13:59,430
ventricular pressure must
be treated specifically.

231
00:14:00,580 --> 00:14:04,030
Also, it is
believed that mitral

232
00:14:04,030 --> 00:14:06,170
annular classification
is associated with

233
00:14:06,170 --> 00:14:08,830
atherosclerotic
disease. Therefore,

234
00:14:09,150 --> 00:14:12,830
the presence of mitral
annular classification should

235
00:14:12,830 --> 00:14:16,170
heighten clinical concern
for concomitant coronary

236
00:14:16,170 --> 00:14:20,250
or antherosclerotic disease
and serve as an opportunity

237
00:14:20,250 --> 00:14:23,430
to address potentially
modifiable cardiovascular

238
00:14:23,430 --> 00:14:27,550
risk factors such as
hypertension and dyslipidemia.

239
00:14:31,150 --> 00:14:34,710
Acid rheumatic fever and
rheumatic heart disease.

240
00:14:35,070 --> 00:14:39,410
Acid rheumatic fever is
immunologically mediated

241
00:14:39,410 --> 00:14:42,690
and represents a multi
-system disease which

242
00:14:42,690 --> 00:14:45,790
affects not only the heart
but also other organs.

243
00:14:47,310 --> 00:14:50,910
Acid rheumatic fever has
an inflammatory character

244
00:14:50,910 --> 00:14:55,410
and develops after pharyngitis
or a skin infection

245
00:14:55,410 --> 00:14:59,350
caused by a group A beta
-hemolytic streptococcus.

246
00:15:00,770 --> 00:15:03,970
Rheumatic heart disease
represents the cardiac

247
00:15:03,970 --> 00:15:07,090
pathology associated with
acute rheumatic fever.

248
00:15:07,470 --> 00:15:10,470
The most important
clinical features are

249
00:15:10,470 --> 00:15:14,090
determined by fibrotic
mitral stenosis.

250
00:15:14,150 --> 00:15:17,630
In fact, rheumatic
heart disease is the

251
00:15:17,630 --> 00:15:20,610
only cause of acquired
mitral stenosis.

252
00:15:24,730 --> 00:15:28,790
Rheumatic fever pathogenesis.
As I mentioned before,

253
00:15:29,090 --> 00:15:31,570
icodraumatic fever
is an immunological

254
00:15:31,570 --> 00:15:34,250
reaction determined
by an infection with

255
00:15:34,250 --> 00:15:36,490
group A beta-hemolytic
streptococcus.

256
00:15:37,110 --> 00:15:40,250
There is a 2-3 weeks
delay in the onset

257
00:15:40,250 --> 00:15:42,870
of clinical features
as the immunological

258
00:15:42,870 --> 00:15:45,270
reaction requires
times for development.

259
00:15:46,100 --> 00:15:48,940
As you can see in this
drawing, the streptococci

260
00:15:48,940 --> 00:15:52,250
have an antigen represented
by the M protein.

261
00:15:52,470 --> 00:15:57,210
The streptococci will
activate beta lymphocytes to

262
00:15:57,210 --> 00:16:00,630
manufacture antibodies
capable of recognizing the

263
00:16:00,630 --> 00:16:05,950
M protein antigen. In
addition, CD4T lymphocytes

264
00:16:05,950 --> 00:16:09,170
are also directed against
streptococcal M protein.

265
00:16:10,780 --> 00:16:13,180
Basically, this
is how the organ

266
00:16:13,180 --> 00:16:15,770
fights against the
bacterial infection.

267
00:16:16,170 --> 00:16:16,990
However,

268
00:16:17,410 --> 00:16:20,650
antibody antigen binding
activates the complement.

269
00:16:20,830 --> 00:16:23,850
This activation
is associated with

270
00:16:24,330 --> 00:16:27,030
recruitment of neutrophils
and macrophages,

271
00:16:27,230 --> 00:16:30,150
further stimulation
of T-cell lymphocytes

272
00:16:30,150 --> 00:16:33,730
leading to cytokine
production, and further

273
00:16:33,730 --> 00:16:36,430
macrophage activation
and tissue damage.

274
00:16:38,010 --> 00:16:41,870
As you can see in this
drawing, all of these would

275
00:16:41,870 --> 00:16:45,310
lead to damage to the
mitral and aortic valves,

276
00:16:45,670 --> 00:16:46,530
arthritis,

277
00:16:46,810 --> 00:16:48,070
and skin involvement.

278
00:16:49,290 --> 00:16:52,990
I would like to highlight
that antibodies and CD4

279
00:16:53,290 --> 00:16:56,190
lymphocytes directed
against streptococcal

280
00:16:56,190 --> 00:17:00,150
M protein recognize
cardiac proteins,

281
00:17:00,570 --> 00:17:04,450
cardiac self-antigens
promoting tissue destruction.

282
00:17:05,150 --> 00:17:08,530
Please note that in
established cases of rheumatic

283
00:17:08,530 --> 00:17:11,450
heart disease, the
streptococci are not seen in

284
00:17:11,450 --> 00:17:14,770
the lesion, as this is an
immunological reaction.

285
00:17:15,450 --> 00:17:19,170
However, as only a
minority estimated at 3%

286
00:17:19,170 --> 00:17:23,130
of patients infected with
group A beta-hemolytic

287
00:17:23,130 --> 00:17:26,590
streptococci develop
acudriomatic fever,

288
00:17:27,070 --> 00:17:30,970
it is likely that the genetic
susceptibility modulates

289
00:17:30,970 --> 00:17:34,610
the development of this
immunological reaction.

290
00:17:37,160 --> 00:17:40,050
I'd like to summarize the
most important clinical

291
00:17:40,050 --> 00:17:44,630
features seen in acudriomatic
fever. As mentioned before,

292
00:17:44,870 --> 00:17:47,670
I could rheumatic fever is
describing a minority of

293
00:17:47,670 --> 00:17:51,570
patients after group A beta
-hemolytic streptococcal

294
00:17:51,570 --> 00:17:54,370
infection and most of
the patients are children

295
00:17:54,370 --> 00:17:58,190
aged between 5 and 15 years
of age. There are five

296
00:17:58,190 --> 00:18:03,650
major diagnostic criteria
joint pain, acute carditis,

297
00:18:03,770 --> 00:18:04,950
nodules,

298
00:18:05,090 --> 00:18:08,730
erythema marginatum
and Sideham chorea.

299
00:18:09,090 --> 00:18:12,450
Let's describe each of
these categories separately.

300
00:18:13,110 --> 00:18:15,850
Acute carditis is
suggested by pericardial

301
00:18:15,850 --> 00:18:19,910
friction rubs and various
types of arrhythmias.

302
00:18:20,160 --> 00:18:22,910
There is myocarditis which

303
00:18:22,910 --> 00:18:24,830
may be seen in some patients

304
00:18:25,110 --> 00:18:27,270
causing cardiac dilatation.

305
00:18:27,450 --> 00:18:30,470
This could culminate
in functional mitral

306
00:18:30,470 --> 00:18:33,420
valve insufficiency
or even heart failure.

307
00:18:33,420 --> 00:18:37,310
About 1% of affected
individuals will

308
00:18:37,310 --> 00:18:40,130
die of fulminant
involvement of the heart

309
00:18:40,850 --> 00:18:44,550
Regarding the joint pain,
this is caused by a migratory

310
00:18:44,550 --> 00:18:48,090
porial arthritis In which
the patient is febrile and

311
00:18:48,090 --> 00:18:51,630
one large joint is affected
after another The joint

312
00:18:51,630 --> 00:18:55,410
becomes painful and swollen
for several days But then

313
00:18:55,410 --> 00:18:58,990
the condition subsides,
leaving no residual disability

314
00:19:00,860 --> 00:19:03,770
On this slide, you see
the typical aspect of

315
00:19:03,770 --> 00:19:06,810
a subcutaneous nodule
associated with an

316
00:19:06,810 --> 00:19:10,030
acridriumatic fever.
These nodules are located

317
00:19:10,030 --> 00:19:13,450
on the extensor surfaces
of fingers or arms.

318
00:19:14,900 --> 00:19:16,890
Also on this slide, you have a

319
00:19:16,890 --> 00:19:19,710
classical example of
Veritema marginato.

320
00:19:19,710 --> 00:19:22,930
This is defined by
large irregular skin

321
00:19:22,930 --> 00:19:26,190
rush areas measuring
several centimeters.

322
00:19:28,490 --> 00:19:31,950
In addition, these patients
present with involuntary

323
00:19:31,950 --> 00:19:35,830
rapid dance-like movements
involving all limbs and

324
00:19:35,830 --> 00:19:40,990
the trunk. This is diagnostic
for Sideham chorea.

325
00:19:46,090 --> 00:19:48,590
Now I would like to
discuss very briefly

326
00:19:48,590 --> 00:19:51,390
the most important
morphological changes

327
00:19:51,390 --> 00:19:53,970
associated with
acuidraumatic fever.

328
00:19:55,110 --> 00:19:56,310
Myocarditis.

329
00:19:57,190 --> 00:19:59,290
Myocarditis is
characterized by the

330
00:19:59,290 --> 00:20:01,290
presence of Ashoff's
bodies, which

331
00:20:01,290 --> 00:20:03,510
are pathognomonic
for this condition.

332
00:20:03,930 --> 00:20:07,770
Ashoff's bodies are
associated with a diffuse

333
00:20:07,770 --> 00:20:11,090
inflammation of the
heart and are composed of

334
00:20:11,090 --> 00:20:14,290
lymphocytes, plasma cells,
and anistikov cells.

335
00:20:14,650 --> 00:20:19,310
Anistikov cells are large
activated macrophages.

336
00:20:19,370 --> 00:20:22,570
It should be noted
that Ashoff's bodies

337
00:20:22,570 --> 00:20:25,150
might be seen not only
myocardium but also

338
00:20:25,150 --> 00:20:28,150
in pericardium and
endocardium and are

339
00:20:28,150 --> 00:20:30,890
indicative of inflammation
of these structures.

340
00:20:31,690 --> 00:20:34,610
This image shows an actual body

341
00:20:34,610 --> 00:20:36,870
in a patient with
acute carditis.

342
00:20:38,430 --> 00:20:43,030
The myocardium shows a
nodule composed of various

343
00:20:43,030 --> 00:20:46,370
types of inflammatory
cells. There is also

344
00:20:46,370 --> 00:20:51,210
necrosis which is indicated
here by a long arrow.

345
00:20:51,490 --> 00:20:55,570
Necrosis appears in
hematoxylin eosin stained slide

346
00:20:55,970 --> 00:21:00,750
as a structureless pinkish
material. The small arrow

347
00:21:01,390 --> 00:21:04,450
identify Anishchikov
cells, large

348
00:21:04,450 --> 00:21:07,430
activated macrophages
with prominent nuclei

349
00:21:07,430 --> 00:21:10,790
and chromatin
condensed into long

350
00:21:10,830 --> 00:21:14,670
wavy ribbon-like
pattern, hence the name

351
00:21:14,670 --> 00:21:17,450
of caterpillar cells
used by some authors

352
00:21:17,450 --> 00:21:20,230
when describing the
Anishchikov cells.

353
00:21:26,420 --> 00:21:29,660
On this slide, the
left side image shows a

354
00:21:29,660 --> 00:21:32,980
classical representation
of the microscopic changes

355
00:21:32,980 --> 00:21:36,420
associated with acridromatic
fever endocarditis.

356
00:21:36,420 --> 00:21:39,060
This is characterized
by irregular

357
00:21:39,060 --> 00:21:42,440
small bifermi-adherent
vegetations along

358
00:21:42,440 --> 00:21:45,320
the closure line of
the mitral valve.

359
00:21:45,500 --> 00:21:49,460
These vegetations are
made of fibrin, and

360
00:21:49,460 --> 00:21:52,820
they probably represent
damage caused by opening

361
00:21:52,820 --> 00:21:55,660
and closing of the
inflamed myocardium.

362
00:21:56,060 --> 00:21:59,560
The right side image
shows an example

363
00:21:59,560 --> 00:22:02,360
of acuidraumatic
fever pericarditis.

364
00:22:02,500 --> 00:22:05,560
The surface of this
heart is covered

365
00:22:05,560 --> 00:22:08,080
by a fibrinous
pericardial exudate

366
00:22:08,080 --> 00:22:11,180
with a bread and
butter-like pattern.

367
00:22:17,750 --> 00:22:20,020
Reumatic heart disease
clinical features.

368
00:22:20,020 --> 00:22:23,350
These features are seen
years or even decades

369
00:22:23,350 --> 00:22:26,210
after initial episode
of acridromatic fever.

370
00:22:26,390 --> 00:22:29,090
In addition to cardiac murmurs,

371
00:22:29,310 --> 00:22:30,810
cardiac hypertrophy,

372
00:22:30,970 --> 00:22:34,550
dilatation and heart failure,
these patients present

373
00:22:34,550 --> 00:22:37,810
with arrhythmias such
as atrial fibrillation,

374
00:22:38,470 --> 00:22:41,710
thromboembolic complications
and endocarditis.

375
00:22:41,930 --> 00:22:45,090
The long-term prognosis
variable from one

376
00:22:45,090 --> 00:22:48,270
patient to the other.
However, surgical repair

377
00:22:48,270 --> 00:22:51,750
and replacement of damaged
valves has significantly

378
00:22:51,750 --> 00:22:54,430
improved the outcome
in these patients.

379
00:22:57,250 --> 00:23:00,590
Heart disease morphology.
While the tricuspid and

380
00:23:00,590 --> 00:23:04,070
pulmonary valves are very
uncommonly affected in rheumatic

381
00:23:04,070 --> 00:23:07,290
heart disease, the mitral
valve is always involved.

382
00:23:07,810 --> 00:23:11,710
Two-thirds of cases present
only with mitral valve

383
00:23:11,710 --> 00:23:15,370
stenosis, While in one
third of the patients,

384
00:23:15,570 --> 00:23:18,490
mitral valve stenosis
is associated with a

385
00:23:18,490 --> 00:23:23,070
pathological aortic valve
The morphology in these

386
00:23:23,070 --> 00:23:27,050
patients is represented
by extensive fibrosis and

387
00:23:27,050 --> 00:23:30,950
calcification Resulting
in severe rheumatic mitral

388
00:23:30,950 --> 00:23:34,670
valve stenosis The so
-called fish mouth stenosis,

389
00:23:34,670 --> 00:23:38,710
which is shown in this
image This type of lesion

390
00:23:38,710 --> 00:23:42,030
induces left outer
hypertrophy and dilatation

391
00:23:42,310 --> 00:23:45,530
A dilated atrium
may harbor moral

392
00:23:45,530 --> 00:23:47,610
thrombi that could embolize.

393
00:23:48,610 --> 00:23:51,470
Anyway, left atrial
dilatation and

394
00:23:51,470 --> 00:23:54,190
hypertrophy, which
appears in time,

395
00:23:54,510 --> 00:23:58,110
determine congestion in
the lungs, leading to

396
00:23:58,110 --> 00:24:01,530
right ventricular hypertrophy
and heart failure.

397
00:24:03,890 --> 00:24:07,430
Infective endocarditis.
This pathological entity

398
00:24:07,430 --> 00:24:10,650
represents a microbial
infection of the heart valves of

399
00:24:10,650 --> 00:24:14,250
moral endocardium leading
to formation of vegetations.

400
00:24:14,530 --> 00:24:17,310
These vegetations are made of

401
00:24:17,310 --> 00:24:20,490
thrombotic debris
and microorganisms.

402
00:24:20,850 --> 00:24:24,070
Apart from heart
valves and endocardium,

403
00:24:24,070 --> 00:24:26,170
aorta and other blood
vessels as well as

404
00:24:26,170 --> 00:24:28,970
prosthetic devices
might become infected.

405
00:24:29,110 --> 00:24:32,630
Most infections in this
setting are bacterial

406
00:24:32,630 --> 00:24:35,050
but fungal infections
are also seen.

407
00:24:36,110 --> 00:24:38,990
Traditionally, infective
endocarditis has been

408
00:24:38,990 --> 00:24:41,830
classified on clinical
grounds into acute and

409
00:24:41,830 --> 00:24:46,590
subacute forms based on
severity and tempo and

410
00:24:46,590 --> 00:24:49,590
whether there is underlying
valvular pathology.

411
00:24:51,370 --> 00:24:55,870
Acute infective endocarditis.
This is caused by

412
00:24:55,870 --> 00:24:58,810
an infection of a previously
normal heart valve

413
00:24:58,810 --> 00:25:03,450
by virulent agents such
as taphylococcus aureus.

414
00:25:03,670 --> 00:25:07,610
The lesions are extensive
in these cases and

415
00:25:07,610 --> 00:25:10,130
it is difficult to
manage the patient and

416
00:25:10,130 --> 00:25:13,070
oftentimes, apart from
antibiotic therapy,

417
00:25:14,030 --> 00:25:16,150
they have to undergo surgery.

418
00:25:16,150 --> 00:25:19,470
Moreover, despite
the best therapy,

419
00:25:20,130 --> 00:25:22,310
morbidity and
mortality are high.

420
00:25:22,490 --> 00:25:24,250
In contrast,

421
00:25:25,070 --> 00:25:29,930
subacute infective endocarditis
is induced by organisms

422
00:25:29,930 --> 00:25:34,110
with lower virulence such
as viridans streptococci.

423
00:25:35,030 --> 00:25:37,390
This causes
insidious infections

424
00:25:37,390 --> 00:25:39,910
of previously deformed valves.

425
00:25:40,350 --> 00:25:44,070
However, there is less
valvular destruction.

426
00:25:44,070 --> 00:25:47,330
The disease may last for
many weeks or months,

427
00:25:47,330 --> 00:25:51,070
but it may be cured only
by antibiotic therapy.

428
00:25:56,380 --> 00:25:58,500
Infective endocarditis
risk factors.

429
00:25:59,740 --> 00:26:02,380
Infective endocarditis
is seen in higher

430
00:26:02,380 --> 00:26:04,980
numbers in patients with
rheumatic heart disease,

431
00:26:04,980 --> 00:26:07,940
mitral valve prolapse
and calcific valvular

432
00:26:07,940 --> 00:26:11,600
stenosis, in those with
prosthetic devices,

433
00:26:11,840 --> 00:26:14,940
in various congenital
heart defects,

434
00:26:14,940 --> 00:26:16,920
and in immunocompromised
patients,

435
00:26:16,920 --> 00:26:20,340
especially in those
with immunodeficiency,

436
00:26:20,720 --> 00:26:22,580
drug abuse disorder,

437
00:26:22,620 --> 00:26:23,780
neutropenia,

438
00:26:24,020 --> 00:26:26,880
malignancy, and
diabetes mellitus.

439
00:26:28,550 --> 00:26:31,160
I would like to summarize
the most important

440
00:26:31,160 --> 00:26:33,820
clinical features in
infective endocarditis.

441
00:26:33,820 --> 00:26:36,420
This condition is
characterized by an abrupt

442
00:26:36,420 --> 00:26:39,940
onset of fever, chills
and general weakness.

443
00:26:40,120 --> 00:26:42,680
All of these signs
are non-specific

444
00:26:42,680 --> 00:26:45,200
but fever is the
most consistent sign.

445
00:26:45,820 --> 00:26:47,460
Fever might not be seen in

446
00:26:47,460 --> 00:26:50,080
older adults.
This older patient

447
00:26:50,200 --> 00:26:53,820
may present only with
weight loss and tiredness.

448
00:26:53,980 --> 00:26:57,740
In addition, murmurs are
also noted in infective

449
00:26:57,740 --> 00:27:00,780
endocarditis and are
determined either by a new

450
00:27:00,780 --> 00:27:04,860
valvular defect or pre
-existing valvular condition.

451
00:27:07,460 --> 00:27:10,180
Infective
endocarditis etiology.

452
00:27:10,500 --> 00:27:14,860
In more than 60% of cases,
infective endocarditis

453
00:27:14,860 --> 00:27:18,800
is induced in a native
valve by Streptococcus

454
00:27:18,800 --> 00:27:21,720
viridans, which is normally
seen in oral cavity.

455
00:27:22,380 --> 00:27:24,940
The native valve
in these cases is

456
00:27:24,940 --> 00:27:28,640
previously damaged or
abnormal. In contrast,

457
00:27:29,260 --> 00:27:31,780
Staphylococcus aureus,
which is found on

458
00:27:31,780 --> 00:27:35,640
the skin, promotes
a virulent infection

459
00:27:35,640 --> 00:27:38,500
of healthy or deformed
valves in up to 20

460
00:27:38,500 --> 00:27:42,560
-30% of all infective
endocarditis cases.

461
00:27:43,940 --> 00:27:47,360
Bacterial endocarditis
may also be determined

462
00:27:47,360 --> 00:27:50,040
by enterococci and
the Hasek group.

463
00:27:50,100 --> 00:27:54,180
Hasek is the abbreviation
for hemophilus,

464
00:27:54,480 --> 00:27:55,900
actinobacillus,

465
00:27:56,440 --> 00:27:57,800
cardiobacterium,

466
00:27:58,080 --> 00:27:59,920
acinella, and kingella.

467
00:28:00,080 --> 00:28:03,700
All of these are normally
seen in oral cavity.

468
00:28:05,060 --> 00:28:08,680
Gram-negative bacilli
and fungi might also

469
00:28:08,680 --> 00:28:11,860
be seen in cases of
infective endocarditis.

470
00:28:12,800 --> 00:28:16,760
A special note for prosthetic
valve endocarditis,

471
00:28:16,860 --> 00:28:20,720
this condition is seen
one to two months after

472
00:28:20,720 --> 00:28:24,600
surgery and is caused
by skin flora such as

473
00:28:24,600 --> 00:28:28,960
staphylococcus aureus or
staphylococcus epidermidis.

474
00:28:29,980 --> 00:28:33,020
Prosthetic valve
endocarditis may also be

475
00:28:33,020 --> 00:28:36,480
diagnosed after more than
one year after surgery,

476
00:28:36,620 --> 00:28:40,460
but these cases are
often associated

477
00:28:40,460 --> 00:28:42,540
with streptococcal infections.

478
00:28:46,080 --> 00:28:50,620
Infective endocarditis
morphology. The most important

479
00:28:50,620 --> 00:28:53,660
morphological hallmark
in infective endocarditis

480
00:28:53,660 --> 00:28:57,260
is represented by the
presence of vegetations.

481
00:28:57,260 --> 00:29:00,720
These are friable bulky
and destructive lesions

482
00:29:00,720 --> 00:29:05,080
containing fibrin inflammatory
cells and microorganisms

483
00:29:05,720 --> 00:29:08,340
the aortic and mitral
valves are frequently

484
00:29:08,340 --> 00:29:11,040
involved although the
valves of the right heart

485
00:29:11,140 --> 00:29:13,200
are affected
especially in those

486
00:29:13,200 --> 00:29:15,980
with iv drug abuse disorder

487
00:29:16,320 --> 00:29:18,460
vegetations are
prone to embolization

488
00:29:18,460 --> 00:29:21,360
in various organs
and parts of the body

489
00:29:22,580 --> 00:29:26,840
In this slide, the image
labeled A shows a case of

490
00:29:26,840 --> 00:29:31,040
subacute endocarditis caused
by Streptococcus viridans.

491
00:29:31,200 --> 00:29:34,300
The heart was opened
longitudinally and you

492
00:29:34,300 --> 00:29:36,940
can see numerous variable
large vegetations on

493
00:29:36,940 --> 00:29:40,680
the mitral valve. The
image labeled B represents

494
00:29:40,680 --> 00:29:44,220
a case of acute
endocarditis of a congenital

495
00:29:44,220 --> 00:29:47,540
by cuspid aortic valve.
This was the final

496
00:29:47,540 --> 00:29:50,420
result of a Staphylococcus
aureus infection.

497
00:29:50,980 --> 00:29:54,300
As you can see, indicated
by the tip of the

498
00:29:54,300 --> 00:29:57,400
forceps, the vegetations
are large, friable,

499
00:29:57,400 --> 00:30:00,480
and there is massive
cuspal destruction

500
00:30:00,480 --> 00:30:03,560
as well as a ring
abscess formation.

501
00:30:04,920 --> 00:30:08,160
Infective endocarditis
histology. As mentioned

502
00:30:08,160 --> 00:30:10,240
before, infective
endocarditis is

503
00:30:10,240 --> 00:30:12,600
characterized by the
presence of vegetations.

504
00:30:12,740 --> 00:30:16,600
In this microscopic picture,
we see a small fragment

505
00:30:16,600 --> 00:30:20,240
of tissue which was taken
from a large-sized vegetation.

506
00:30:20,300 --> 00:30:23,800
This lesion is comprised
of fibrin and platelets.

507
00:30:24,020 --> 00:30:27,440
Also, as indicated by
the tip of the arrow,

508
00:30:27,520 --> 00:30:30,380
the superficial layer
of this structure

509
00:30:30,380 --> 00:30:33,580
contains inflammatory
cells and bacteria which

510
00:30:33,580 --> 00:30:36,100
appear darker than the
rest of the lesion.

511
00:30:36,860 --> 00:30:40,280
I would like to discuss
some clinical signs

512
00:30:40,280 --> 00:30:43,800
which are diagnostic for
infective endocarditis.

513
00:30:44,600 --> 00:30:46,260
Janeway's lesions.

514
00:30:46,260 --> 00:30:49,680
These are small erythematous
or hemorrhagic micular

515
00:30:49,680 --> 00:30:54,160
non-tender lesions seen
on palms and soles. They

516
00:30:54,160 --> 00:30:57,270
result from embolization
of friable vegetations.

517
00:30:57,960 --> 00:31:01,880
Small friable fragments
become dislodged and

518
00:31:01,880 --> 00:31:05,440
subsequently end up in
a terminal blood vessel.

519
00:31:06,160 --> 00:31:07,900
Rot spots.

520
00:31:08,060 --> 00:31:10,640
These are oval
retinal hemorrhages

521
00:31:10,640 --> 00:31:14,120
with pale centers
seen in only 2% of

522
00:31:14,120 --> 00:31:16,400
patients with
effective endocarditis.

523
00:31:16,600 --> 00:31:18,960
They result after
embolization of

524
00:31:18,960 --> 00:31:20,840
small fragments of vegetations.

525
00:31:20,960 --> 00:31:24,080
However, some authors
claim that these

526
00:31:24,080 --> 00:31:26,500
lesions might have an
immunological cause.

527
00:31:28,720 --> 00:31:31,440
Nailbed or splinter
hemorrhages.

528
00:31:32,320 --> 00:31:36,440
They also result from
embolization of small

529
00:31:36,440 --> 00:31:39,380
friable fragments of
vegetations which end

530
00:31:39,380 --> 00:31:42,320
up in the small vessels
of the nail bed.

531
00:31:43,880 --> 00:31:48,300
Osler nodes. These are
small tender subcutaneous

532
00:31:48,300 --> 00:31:52,780
nodules that develop in the
pulp of the digits or at

533
00:31:52,780 --> 00:31:55,840
the level of interphalangeal
joints of the fingers.

534
00:31:57,200 --> 00:32:00,520
They can last from
hours to days.

535
00:32:00,760 --> 00:32:05,760
The underlying cause of
these nodules is debatable.

536
00:32:06,060 --> 00:32:09,140
Early reports favored an
allergic or immunological

537
00:32:09,140 --> 00:32:11,800
cause, but more
recent studies have

538
00:32:11,800 --> 00:32:15,020
isolated bacteria from
within the nodules.

539
00:32:15,080 --> 00:32:18,640
Therefore, it is believed
that they result from

540
00:32:18,640 --> 00:32:22,400
embolization of small
vegetation fragments.

541
00:32:25,680 --> 00:32:30,040
Non-bacterial thrombotic
endocarditis. This

542
00:32:30,040 --> 00:32:33,260
condition is characterized
by deposition of small 1

543
00:32:33,260 --> 00:32:37,300
to 5 mm sterile thrombi
on the valvular leaflets.

544
00:32:37,640 --> 00:32:41,760
Frequently, non-bacterial
thrombotic endocarditis

545
00:32:41,760 --> 00:32:44,180
is seen in cancers
such as mucinous

546
00:32:44,180 --> 00:32:48,400
adenocarcinomas. It is also
seen in patients with severe

547
00:32:48,400 --> 00:32:52,200
infections or sepsis
including those with

548
00:32:52,200 --> 00:32:55,700
hypercoagulable states
such as disseminated

549
00:32:55,700 --> 00:33:00,000
intravascular coagulation
and hyperestrogenic states.

550
00:33:00,200 --> 00:33:03,800
In all these clinical
settings the patients

551
00:33:03,800 --> 00:33:07,800
present with normal valves
but endocardial trauma

552
00:33:07,800 --> 00:33:11,560
from an indwelling
catheter is also a risk

553
00:33:11,560 --> 00:33:15,140
factor for non-bacterial
thrombotic endocarditis.

554
00:33:15,610 --> 00:33:19,120
On the left side of this
slide, there are two images.

555
00:33:19,400 --> 00:33:23,140
Image A shows a
longitudinally dissected heart

556
00:33:23,140 --> 00:33:26,960
with a row of thrombotic
vegetations along

557
00:33:26,960 --> 00:33:29,560
the line of closure
of the mitral valve

558
00:33:29,560 --> 00:33:33,080
leaflets. These vegetations
are non destructive

559
00:33:33,080 --> 00:33:36,640
and do not cause an
inflammatory reaction.

560
00:33:37,020 --> 00:33:40,100
However, they can
embolize, causing

561
00:33:40,100 --> 00:33:42,360
infarcts in the brain,
heart and kidneys.

562
00:33:44,130 --> 00:33:48,700
Image B represents the
microscopic structure of a

563
00:33:48,700 --> 00:33:52,160
sterile vegetation,
characteristic for non-bacterial

564
00:33:52,160 --> 00:33:55,280
thrombotic endocarditis.
There is no inflammatory

565
00:33:55,280 --> 00:33:59,000
infiltrate in the valve cuts,
which can be seen in the

566
00:33:59,000 --> 00:34:03,220
left side of this image. The
thrombotic sterile material

567
00:34:03,220 --> 00:34:06,060
is very loosely attached
to the valvular surface.

568
00:34:06,480 --> 00:34:09,800
And this is composed
only of fibrin,

569
00:34:09,800 --> 00:34:12,340
platelets and other
blood components.

570
00:34:14,240 --> 00:34:17,660
Liebman Sachs
endocarditis. This type of

571
00:34:17,660 --> 00:34:22,040
endocarditis is seen in
systemic lupus erythematosus,

572
00:34:22,040 --> 00:34:24,760
which is an
immunological condition.

573
00:34:25,540 --> 00:34:29,580
It is characterized by
small 1 to 4 mm sterile

574
00:34:29,580 --> 00:34:33,080
vegetations. These
vegetations result from immune

575
00:34:33,080 --> 00:34:36,140
complex deposition with
activation of complement.

576
00:34:36,520 --> 00:34:39,740
The vegetations
are seen anywhere

577
00:34:39,740 --> 00:34:41,640
on the valvular surfaces,

578
00:34:41,860 --> 00:34:44,340
on corded tendon, or on

579
00:34:44,340 --> 00:34:46,320
atrial and ventricular septum.

580
00:34:46,580 --> 00:34:49,900
These lesions might
promote fibrosis,

581
00:34:49,900 --> 00:34:53,240
scarring, and fusion of
the valvular leaflets.

582
00:34:53,860 --> 00:34:57,760
The right side image
represents a dissected

583
00:34:57,760 --> 00:35:01,430
heart showing several
pink sterile vegetations

584
00:35:01,430 --> 00:35:04,480
along the line of
closure of mitral valve.

585
00:35:04,720 --> 00:35:08,720
The left side microscopic
image shows a section

586
00:35:08,720 --> 00:35:11,960
of the mitral valve
leaflet vegetation

587
00:35:11,960 --> 00:35:15,560
stained with hematoxylin
eosin. There is

588
00:35:15,560 --> 00:35:18,900
inflammation of the valve
or valvulitis indicated

589
00:35:18,900 --> 00:35:22,020
by the presence of
neutrophils and monocytes.

590
00:35:22,260 --> 00:35:25,620
On the upper right
side of this image,

591
00:35:25,620 --> 00:35:28,760
you might see fibrinoid
necrosis, composed

592
00:35:28,760 --> 00:35:31,540
of fine eosinophilic
acellular material.

593
00:35:31,880 --> 00:35:35,420
No micro-organes are
seen in this lesion.

594
00:35:38,900 --> 00:35:42,740
On the last slide of
today's lecture, there is a

595
00:35:42,740 --> 00:35:45,620
summary which might help
you during your studies.

596
00:35:46,260 --> 00:35:49,360
Initially, we have
described the most salient

597
00:35:49,360 --> 00:35:53,760
features of valvular disease
and then we have discussed

598
00:35:53,760 --> 00:35:57,280
the most important forms
of aortic stenosis,

599
00:35:57,280 --> 00:36:01,020
the calcific aortic stenosis
and the aortic stenosis

600
00:36:01,020 --> 00:36:05,580
which develops in a
congenital bicuspid valve.

601
00:36:06,460 --> 00:36:10,940
Currently it is accepted
that aortic stenosis is

602
00:36:10,940 --> 00:36:15,240
caused by the age-related
wear and tear which is

603
00:36:15,240 --> 00:36:18,190
the equivalent of age
-related atherosclerosis.

604
00:36:19,200 --> 00:36:21,580
Then we have
defined mitral valve

605
00:36:21,580 --> 00:36:24,380
prolapse and mitral
annular calcification.

606
00:36:24,580 --> 00:36:28,640
The first one is
myxomatous degeneration or

607
00:36:28,640 --> 00:36:32,020
deposition in the mitral
valve leaflets of an

608
00:36:32,020 --> 00:36:35,340
abnormal material
reaching proteoglycans.

609
00:36:35,340 --> 00:36:38,860
Mitral annular calcification
on the other side

610
00:36:39,160 --> 00:36:44,840
is abnormal deposition
of calcium in the mitral

611
00:36:44,840 --> 00:36:50,920
fibrous annulus. Then
we have discussed the

612
00:36:50,920 --> 00:36:54,120
acuidraumatic fever versus
rheumatic heart disease.

613
00:36:54,540 --> 00:36:57,700
Acuidraumatic fever
is considered an

614
00:36:57,700 --> 00:37:00,500
immunological reaction
determined by a group

615
00:37:00,500 --> 00:37:03,280
A beta-hemolytic
streptococcal infection.

616
00:37:03,940 --> 00:37:07,610
Most of the time
it's a pharyngitis.

617
00:37:07,840 --> 00:37:10,540
We have presented
the histological

618
00:37:10,540 --> 00:37:13,620
hallmarks of
acuidraumatic fever, the

619
00:37:13,620 --> 00:37:16,380
ash of bodies and
the anistikov cells.

620
00:37:16,900 --> 00:37:21,200
Also, we have defined the
major clinical criteria,

621
00:37:21,200 --> 00:37:25,860
and we have explained in
detail the related carditis.

622
00:37:26,820 --> 00:37:32,060
Also, we have debated the
morphology of rheumatic

623
00:37:32,060 --> 00:37:35,700
heart disease, which was
presented in contrast

624
00:37:35,700 --> 00:37:39,240
with acute rheumatic
fever. It was highlighted

625
00:37:39,240 --> 00:37:42,060
that rheumatic heart
disease is the only cause

626
00:37:42,060 --> 00:37:47,420
of acquired mitral
stenosis. Then, we have

627
00:37:47,420 --> 00:37:50,500
presented the acute and
subacute forms of infective

628
00:37:50,500 --> 00:37:53,740
endocarditis and their
etiological factors.

629
00:37:54,360 --> 00:37:58,460
Histologically,
infective endocarditis is

630
00:37:58,460 --> 00:38:01,300
remarkable by the
presence of large friable

631
00:38:01,300 --> 00:38:05,140
vegetations containing
fibrin and platelets

632
00:38:05,140 --> 00:38:07,880
mixed with inflammatory
cells and bacteria.

633
00:38:08,440 --> 00:38:12,060
In this lecture, we
have also explained the

634
00:38:12,060 --> 00:38:15,620
appearance of infecting
endocarditis clinical

635
00:38:15,620 --> 00:38:19,560
features, such as genoay
lesions, rot spots,

636
00:38:20,000 --> 00:38:23,580
nail bed or splinter
hemorrhages, and Osler nodules.

637
00:38:24,640 --> 00:38:28,160
Also, we have defined the
non-bacterial thrombotic

638
00:38:28,160 --> 00:38:31,100
endocarditis, which
is associated with

639
00:38:31,100 --> 00:38:34,240
cancers, such as mucinous
adenocarcinoma. carcinoma.

640
00:38:34,240 --> 00:38:38,580
It is also seen in
hypercoagulable states.

641
00:38:39,060 --> 00:38:42,480
This condition is
notable for its non

642
00:38:42,480 --> 00:38:47,060
-bacterial, sterile
vegetation, composed only of

643
00:38:47,060 --> 00:38:50,180
fibrin, platelets,
and blood components.

644
00:38:50,650 --> 00:38:52,880
These vegetations are friable

645
00:38:52,880 --> 00:38:55,240
and can easily embolize.

646
00:38:55,540 --> 00:39:00,120
In the end, we
have discussed the

647
00:39:00,120 --> 00:39:04,140
Leibmann-Sax
endocarditis, which is a

648
00:39:04,140 --> 00:39:07,080
feature of systemic
lupus erythematosus.

649
00:39:07,520 --> 00:39:11,000
This is an immunological
condition and

650
00:39:11,000 --> 00:39:13,540
the resulting vegetations
are seen on any

651
00:39:13,540 --> 00:39:17,400
valve surface or
region of endocardium.

652
00:39:18,720 --> 00:39:22,540
In Leibmann-Sax
endocarditis, vegetations

653
00:39:22,690 --> 00:39:26,140
occur as a result
of activation of

654
00:39:26,140 --> 00:39:29,280
complement with imun
complex deposition.

655
00:39:30,260 --> 00:39:32,360
Thank you very much
for your attention

656
00:39:33,010 --> 00:39:35,200
and good luck
with your studies.

657
00:39:35,740 --> 00:39:36,760
Bye-bye.